From 81074f7d9e8effe745c5b1e1fde5c5bcd695d7d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 14:35:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: translate countdown "Private Reservation" label and
 subtext
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The countdown component (the big timer + "Private Reservation" label
shown on every proposal) had its own hardcoded English strings,
completely bypassing next-intl — confirmed on a live proposal, "Private
Reservation" and its subtext stayed in English even after everything
else on the page was translated correctly.

- Countdown.tsx now uses useTranslations("proposal") for the label
  (reuses the existing reservation.label key already used elsewhere on
  the page) and two new keys (reservation.countdownDescription,
  reservation.redirecting) for its specific subtext/redirect message.
- Found two more hardcoded "Private Reservation" instances in the
  proposal page's no-match and expired states, and one in
  booking-confirmed/page.tsx — wired all three to the same key via
  getTranslations("proposal") (moved to the top of the proposal page's
  component so it's available before the early returns).
- proposalConfig.ts also has a "Private Reservation" string, but
  confirmed it's dead code (never read by ProposalHero, the only
  component that imports proposalConfig) — left alone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XBj5YyCv7itzLP8BDyrEj5
